{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>His garments.</b> He dressed him in the garments of the high priesthood and stripped them off him, to put them on his son in his presence. He said to him: Enter the cave — and he entered. He saw a bed spread and a lamp burning. He said to him: Ascend onto the bed — and he ascended. Stretch out your hands — and he stretched. Close your mouth — and he closed. Close your eyes — and he closed. Immediately Moses longed for that death, and this is what is said to him: ״כַּאֲשֶׁר מֵת אַהֲרֹן אָחִיךָ״ (Deuteronomy 32) — the death you longed for (Sifrei ad loc.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:48.134265787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}